2025-05-19 17:09:59,180 - INFO - {"id": "chatcmpl-BYwOU7rOJhIsrP7BiqKurDqTqshNd", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "Thought: I need to extract market forces from the HTML I just received.\n\nExtract all market forces related to 'Global Market Forces affecting the Banking Sector' found in this text. Structure the output for just these forces according to the RawMarketForce fields needed (title, raw_description, source_name, source_url, source_date, key_terms, etc.).\n\nI now know the final answer\n\nFinal Answer: {\n  \"source_category\": \"Various\",\n  \"source_title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n  \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n  \"summary\": \"This analysis extracted 7 distinct global market forces from Deloitte's 2025 Banking and Capital Markets Outlook (published 13 October 2024). The forces span macroeconomic, regulatory, technological, and competitive domains, each with persistent, measurable impact on the banking sector globally. All forces are externally driven, have medium- to long-term momentum, and are substantiated by findings, statistics, and examples from the source. No content was found specific to First Abu Dhabi Bank. All required fields are present and validated.\",\n  \"raw_market_forces\": [\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf1\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Macroeconomic and Geopolitical Uncertainty\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"Persistent macroeconomic and geopolitical uncertainties\u2014including subpar economic growth, fluctuating interest rates, inflation, and ongoing geopolitical shocks\u2014are expected to keep bank executives vigilant. These forces influence consumer spending, business investment, and overall financial stability, requiring banks to adapt to a low-growth, low-rate environment. The impact is global, with varying effects across regions and direct implications for loan demand, deposit costs, and credit quality.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"macroeconomic uncertainty\", \"geopolitical shocks\", \"interest rates\", \"inflation\", \"economic growth\", \"consumer spending\", \"business investment\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"Deloitte\", \"Federal Reserve\", \"European Central Bank\", \"Bank of England\", \"Bank of Canada\", \"Bank of Japan\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Bank executives will be welcoming 2025 with mixed emotions, unsure how the year will unfold and reshape banks\u2019 fortunes. While inflationary pressures have subsided and interest rates are dropping, subpar economic growth, continuing geopolitical shocks, and regulatory uncertainty will likely give bank CEOs anxiety.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The US economy will likely have performed better than expected in 2024, with annual GDP growth estimated to end at 2.7%. However, in 2025, economic growth is expected to decelerate and interest rates to drop meaningfully.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Total consumer debt is now at an all-time high and has shot up to US$17.7 trillion as of second quarter 2024.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"US GDP likely to grow at 1.5% in its baseline scenario for 2025; Consumer Price Index expected to get closer to the 2% target rate.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Aggregate savings are declining: pandemic-era excess savings were fully depleted by March 2024.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Macroeconomic and geopolitical uncertainties should keep bank executives on their toes.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"Decelerating economic growth\", \"Interest rate volatility\", \"Rising consumer debt\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"Global economic uncertainty\", \"Geopolitical instability\"],\n      \"possible_signals\": [\"Rising unemployment\", \"Weak business investment\"],\n      \"possible_structural_shifts\": [\"Shift to lower growth and lower rate environment\"],\n      \"implications_on_future_of_sector\": [\n        \"Banks must adapt to persistent uncertainty and volatility.\",\n        \"Strategic planning must account for rapid changes in macroeconomic conditions.\"\n      ],\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"date\": \"13 October 2024\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf2\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Regulatory Change and Basel III Endgame\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"Ongoing regulatory changes, especially the Basel III Endgame re-proposal, are reshaping capital requirements and risk management for banks globally. The evolving regulatory landscape introduces uncertainty, compels banks to optimize capital, and may drive M&A activity, especially among midsize and regional banks. Divergence in regulatory implementation across jurisdictions (US, UK, EU) may affect global competitiveness and strategic positioning.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"Basel III\", \"regulatory change\", \"capital requirements\", \"risk management\", \"M&A\", \"regulatory divergence\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"Federal Reserve\", \"FDIC\", \"OCC\", \"Prudential Regulatory Authority\", \"EU Commission\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The Basel III Endgame re-proposal suggests lower capital requirements than the original proposal; however, these rules have not yet been finalized. Banks are likely to continue decreasing their excess capital to optimize their balance sheets, as well as engage in financial transactions to reduce capital needs.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The Federal Reserve\u2019s re-proposal may prompt other regulators to delay and soften their own rules. For instance, the United Kingdom has postponed its implementation date to January 2026.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Banks are redeeming preferred shares to reduce capital and boost return on equity.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Changes are collectively estimated to result in a 9% increase in common equity tier 1 for global systemically important banks (GSIBs).\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Banks with assets between US$10 billion to US$100 billion have the highest CRE loans as a percentage of risk-based capital (199% as of second quarter 2024).\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Other countries are adopting their own Basel III requirements, which may impact bank competitiveness around the world.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"Regulatory divergence\", \"Capital optimization\", \"Increased M&A activity\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"Global regulatory harmonization\", \"Financial system resilience\"],\n      \"possible_signals\": [\"Delays in regulatory implementation\", \"Changes in capital structure\"],\n      \"possible_structural_shifts\": [\"Shift in global banking competitiveness\", \"Rise of nonbank financial institutions\"],\n      \"implications_on_future_of_sector\": [\n        \"Banks must remain agile in response to evolving regulatory standards.\",\n        \"Strategic M&A and capital management will be critical for compliance and competitiveness.\"\n      ],\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"date\": \"13 October 2024\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf3\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Technological Modernization and AI Adoption\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"Rapid advancements in AI and digital technologies are transforming banking operations, customer engagement, and risk management. The push to become AI-powered is global, with banks investing in cloud migration, data infrastructure, and automation. However, legacy systems and technical debt remain significant barriers. The adoption of both traditional and generative AI is expected to accelerate, with implications for productivity, cost management, and competitive differentiation.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"AI\", \"digital transformation\", \"cloud migration\", \"data infrastructure\", \"automation\", \"technical debt\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"JPMorgan\", \"BAC Community Bank\", \"Citigroup\", \"Deloitte AI Institute\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The transformative potential of AI in banking is swiftly becoming a reality. Rapid advancements in both traditional and cutting-edge AI technologies are set to revolutionize the delivery and consumption of banking services.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"JPMorgan is investing in generative AI and other emerging technologies, such as quantum computing. BAC Community Bank launched an AI-powered app that answers user questions and assigns a nearby banker to serve as their point of contact.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Only one-quarter of banking respondents said their data management platforms are highly or very highly prepared to adopt generative AI tools and applications.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"AI could propel global banking industry profits to a staggering US$2 trillion by 2028, reflecting a 9% increase over the next five years.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"More than three-quarters of banks plan to increase investments in data management and cloud consumption to advance their enterprisewide generative AI strategy.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The promise of an AI-powered bank can serve as a catalyst to accelerate technology modernization.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"AI adoption\", \"Cloud migration\", \"Legacy system modernization\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"Digital transformation\", \"Automation\"],\n      \"possible_signals\": [\"Increased AI pilot projects\", \"Cloud investment announcements\"],\n      \"possible_structural_shifts\": [\"Shift to AI-powered banking\", \"Decline of legacy systems\"],\n      \"implications_on_future_of_sector\": [\n        \"Banks that modernize technology and adopt AI will gain competitive advantage.\",\n        \"Failure to address technical debt may hinder growth and innovation.\"\n      ],\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"date\": \"13 October 2024\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf4\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Cost Pressures and Efficiency Imperative\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"Persistent cost pressures from rising compensation, regulatory compliance, and technology investments are forcing banks to prioritize sustainable cost management. Despite efforts, many banks struggle to achieve long-term cost reductions due to challenges with technology infrastructure and operational inefficiencies. The imperative to improve efficiency ratios and control expenses is global, with European banks facing particularly acute pressures.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"cost management\", \"efficiency ratio\", \"compensation\", \"regulatory compliance\", \"technology investment\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"Citigroup\", \"Truist\", \"Deutsche Bank\", \"Standard Chartered\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Banks are struggling to get their costs under control, and the imperative to bring down expenses should only intensify as revenue growth is expected to remain elusive in 2025.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Citigroup is taking drastic steps to simplify its organizational structure and exit noncore markets, in part to manage expenses. Truist aims to improve operating leverage by restructuring businesses, consolidating its branch network, and rationalizing headcount.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Among US banks with more than US$10 billion in assets, compensation expenses grew 4.1% year over year, to US$149.6 billion in the first half of 2024.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The industry\u2019s average efficiency ratio may hover around 60% in 2025.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"In 2024, 15 out of 26 large European banks are expected to see cost growth surpass revenue growth.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Expense management will be a major priority; banks will need to focus on pulling the right levers to keep costs under control and, at the same time, help pave the way for sustainable growth.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"Rising compensation\", \"Regulatory compliance costs\", \"Efficiency initiatives\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"Cost optimization\", \"Operational efficiency\"],\n      \"possible_signals\": [\"Expense target revisions\", \"Branch consolidation\"],\n      \"possible_structural_shifts\": [\"Shift to leaner operating models\", \"Increased automation\"],\n      \"implications_on_future_of_sector\": [\n        \"Banks must embed cost discipline and transparency for sustainable profitability.\",\n        \"Failure to control costs may erode competitiveness and shareholder value.\"\n      ],\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"date\": \"13 October 2024\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf5\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Changing Consumer Behavior and Demand Patterns\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"Shifts in consumer behavior\u2014including declining aggregate savings, rising debt, and changing preferences for digital and value-added services\u2014are impacting loan demand, deposit mix, and fee income strategies. Banks must adapt to evolving customer expectations, increased price sensitivity, and the need for personalized, digital-first experiences. These trends are global and persistent, influencing product design and revenue models.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"consumer behavior\", \"digital banking\", \"fee income\", \"personalization\", \"customer experience\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\", \"Adyen\", \"Mastercard\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The strength of the American consumer will be tested in 2025. Consumer spending could fall as consumer debt weighs on finances. Total consumer debt is now at an all-time high and has shot up to US$17.7 trillion as of second quarter 2024.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"A recent study by Adyen found that 55% of surveyed customers will abandon a purchase if they cannot pay with the instrument of their choice.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The CFPB has proposed a cap on overdraft fees as low as US$3.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Noninterest income as a percentage of average assets is estimated to increase to nearly 1.5%, the highest in the last five years.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Only 36% of wealth management clients surveyed were happy with their fee structures, with wealthier clients being the least satisfied.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Banks should focus more on boosting noninterest income to compensate for challenges in growing net interest income.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"Digital-first banking\", \"Fee compression\", \"Personalized services\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"Consumer empowerment\", \"Digital transformation\"],\n      \"possible_signals\": [\"Declining branch visits\", \"Increased digital engagement\"],\n      \"possible_structural_shifts\": [\"Shift to digital and value-added services\", \"Redesign of fee structures\"],\n      \"implications_on_future_of_sector\": [\n        \"Banks must innovate in product design and customer engagement.\",\n        \"Failure to adapt to changing consumer preferences may result in lost market share.\"\n      ],\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"date\": \"13 October 2024\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf6\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Competitive Dynamics and Nonbank Financial Institutions\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"The rise of nonbank financial institutions, fintechs, and bigtechs is intensifying competition in lending, payments, and value-added services. Banks face margin compression, loss of market share, and the need to innovate rapidly. This competitive pressure is global and persistent, driving banks to seek partnerships, invest in technology, and diversify revenue streams.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"nonbank financial institutions\", \"fintech\", \"bigtech\", \"competition\", \"innovation\", \"partnerships\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"KeyCorp\", \"Huntington Bancshares\", \"Ally Financial\", \"Mastercard\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Banks face increased lending competition from nonbank financial institutions. Increased capital requirements raise the cost of lending for banks, which are adapting to the growth of private credit.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"KeyCorp has arranged a deal to transfer its card portfolio to an alternative asset manager.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Payments business is facing challenges like declining transaction margins and greater regulatory pressure on credit card late fees. Merchants are incentivizing customers to use low-cost payment methods.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Fee income generates well over US$100 billion for US payments companies.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Payment networks earn almost all their revenues and profits from fees.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Competition from bigtechs and fintechs is also growing.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"Fintech disruption\", \"Private credit growth\", \"Partnership models\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"Digital competition\", \"Platformization\"],\n      \"possible_signals\": [\"Bank-fintech partnerships\", \"Asset transfers to nonbanks\"],\n      \"possible_structural_shifts\": [\"Disintermediation of traditional banks\", \"Rise of platform-based financial services\"],\n      \"implications_on_future_of_sector\": [\n        \"Banks must innovate and partner to remain competitive.\",\n        \"Failure to respond to nonbank competition may erode profitability.\"\n      ],\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"2025 banking and capital markets outlook\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"date\": \"13 October 2024\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"raw_market_force_id\": \"mf7\",\n      \"raw_market_force_name\": \"Credit Quality and Commercial Real Estate Risks\",\n      \"raw_description\": \"Credit quality is expected to normalize but could edge higher in 2025, with rising delinquencies and net charge-offs, especially in consumer loans and commercial real estate (CRE). The CRE sector, particularly office space, remains distressed, posing risks for regional banks. These credit risks are persistent and have significant implications for balance sheet management, capital allocation, and regulatory scrutiny.\",\n      \"key_terms\": [\"credit quality\", \"delinquencies\", \"net charge-offs\", \"commercial real estate\", \"CRE\", \"balance sheet risk\"],\n      \"mentioned_entities\": [\"Deloitte\", \"Federal Reserve\"],\n      \"raw_findings\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Credit quality overall is expected to return to normal, with delinquencies and net charge-offs increasing modestly from 2024 levels. The commercial real estate (CRE) sector, particularly the office segment, continues to remain in distress, with regional banks possibly facing the brunt of potential loan losses.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"raw_examples\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Credit card loans have the highest 90+ day delinquency rate among all loan categories (1.69% as of second quarter 2024), and the highest net charge-off rates (4% as of second quarter 2024).\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_facts\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Banks with assets between US$10 billion to US$100 billion have the highest CRE loans as a percentage of risk-based capital (199% as of second quarter 2024).\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_statistics\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The overall net charge-off rate is expected to reach 0.66% in 2025, the highest in the last decade but significantly lower than the 2008\u20132009 crisis (2.6%).\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_data\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"Delinquencies will likely rise in credit card and auto loans as consumers\u2019 balance sheets weaken.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relevant_quotes\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"The commercial real estate (CRE) sector, particularly the office segment, continues to remain in distress, with regional banks possibly facing the brunt of potential loan losses.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/industry/financial-services/financial-services-industry-outlooks/banking-industry-outlook.html\",\n          \"source_text\": null,\n          \"source_name\": \"Deloitte\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"related_trends\": [\"Rising delinquencies\", \"CRE distress\", \"Consumer loan risk\"],\n      \"related_mega_trends\": [\"C